A(('p', '13.3 Final Synthesis. Luke says Jesus told the parable because He was nigh to Jerusalem and they thought the kingdom of God should immediately appear. A certain nobleman went into a far country to receive a kingdom and to return, and he gave ten pounds to ten servants with the charge “Occupy till I come.” His citizens sent a message that they would not have him to reign over them. He returned, having received the kingdom, and gave authority over ten cities and five cities to the servants who had gained, and took the pound from the one who had laid it up in a napkin. He commanded that his enemies be brought and slain before him. Jesus gives no explanation and names none of the parts. The comparison says that a trust is committed before the going away, that the return brings a reckoning, that faithfulness in a little is given authority, and that what is laid up unused is taken away.'))
